1
00:00:00,269 --> 00:00:01,976
It’s obvious someone has him killed.

2
00:00:03,560 --> 00:00:05,736
I’ll take care of the Kitti case myself.

3
00:00:05,780 --> 00:00:07,130
Why didn’t you tell me?

4
00:00:07,237 --> 00:00:09,720
You were one of the investigators
on the Thai Investment Bank case.

5
00:00:09,814 --> 00:00:11,777
Are you suggesting Thun is Asura?

6
00:00:11,950 --> 00:00:12,797
Thunwikorn.

7
00:00:13,202 --> 00:00:16,970
His parents got swindled
by the Thai Investment Bank.

8
00:00:17,040 --> 00:00:18,342
They ended their own lives.

9
00:00:18,390 --> 00:00:19,920
This could be his motivation.

10
00:00:20,041 --> 00:00:21,900
His life isn’t all that different from mine.

11
00:00:24,150 --> 00:00:26,096
It has to be something you can guess.

12
00:00:26,274 --> 00:00:28,797
And it must be something
only you and he know.

13
00:00:29,004 --> 00:00:33,068
The ending of Nekros
was just uploaded minutes ago.

14
00:00:33,150 --> 00:00:34,810
The worst thing is…

15
00:00:35,056 --> 00:00:38,696
when law enforcers themselves
are the bad guys.

16
00:00:39,502 --> 00:00:43,280
Your sister came over to visit your uncle
about an hour ago.

17
00:00:43,320 --> 00:00:46,000
If it wasn’t for Nekros,
you’d have found Prim and me as corpses.

18
00:00:46,110 --> 00:00:50,201
There’s a type of murderer
called a mastermind.

19
00:00:50,510 --> 00:00:52,297
He wouldn’t get his hands bloodied.

20
00:00:52,620 --> 00:00:54,548
He borrows someone else’s hands
to do his dirty work.

21
00:01:01,270 --> 00:01:02,640
But don’t worry.

22
00:01:03,180 --> 00:01:05,296
I’ll do anything to prove

23
00:01:06,096 --> 00:01:07,530
that you’re innocent.

24
00:01:08,582 --> 00:01:09,497
So…

25
00:01:10,580 --> 00:01:12,000
What can I do?

26
00:01:13,930 --> 00:01:15,065
Just stay here.

27
00:01:16,300 --> 00:01:17,302
Don’t go anywhere.

28
00:01:18,157 --> 00:01:19,300
I’ll be back soon.

29
00:01:19,762 --> 00:01:20,494
Okay?

30
00:01:22,670 --> 00:01:23,468
Phat…

31
00:01:26,105 --> 00:01:27,897
Will you promise me one thing?

32
00:01:29,540 --> 00:01:32,798
You… will protect the innocent.

33
00:01:34,260 --> 00:01:36,700
And you won’t let anyone
go through what I did.

34
00:01:41,120 --> 00:01:41,976
I promise.

35
00:01:43,757 --> 00:01:46,697
Even if it costs me my life, I’ll do it.

36
00:01:49,390 --> 00:01:50,297
Alright?

37
00:01:52,158 --> 00:01:53,099
Now eat your breakfast.

38
00:03:47,360 --> 00:03:48,300
To all units,

39
00:03:48,734 --> 00:03:50,610
the car approaching belongs to
the commissioner’s relative.

40
00:03:50,897 --> 00:03:52,091
No need to check her identity.

41
00:03:52,131 --> 00:03:53,410
Back to your station.

42
00:04:20,520 --> 00:04:22,299
You haven’t gone to bed, have you, Uncle?

43
00:04:22,499 --> 00:04:24,530
I bought you some swallow nests,
your favorite.

44
00:04:24,862 --> 00:04:27,410
I was afraid you might have gone to bed
so I came here in a rush.

45
00:04:28,200 --> 00:04:30,000
I was just craving it.

46
00:04:30,325 --> 00:04:31,410
You read my mind.

47
00:04:31,834 --> 00:04:33,804
That’s good. I’ll serve it.

48
00:04:46,118 --> 00:04:48,850
It makes me happy
to see you smile again, Praew.

49
00:04:49,300 --> 00:04:51,497
What’s past is past.

50
00:04:52,962 --> 00:04:54,102
You should eat.

51
00:04:54,257 --> 00:04:55,720
It won’t taste good when it’s cold.

52
00:05:02,010 --> 00:05:02,800
Hmm.

53
00:05:14,608 --> 00:05:15,299
Uncle.

54
00:05:15,850 --> 00:05:19,737
I read online that you’re going to be
Nekros’ last victim.

55
00:05:22,204 --> 00:05:24,297
I wouldn’t worry about that nonsense.

56
00:05:24,820 --> 00:05:26,500
I have work to do.

57
00:05:30,274 --> 00:05:33,700
Are you certain about that
because the case happened long ago,

58
00:05:33,949 --> 00:05:36,560
and you thought there was nothing
that would lead to you?

59
00:05:40,431 --> 00:05:41,197
Praew.

60
00:05:42,630 --> 00:05:43,703
What are you saying?

61
00:06:00,850 --> 00:06:01,600
Praew…

62
00:06:53,382 --> 00:06:55,200
I’m sorry. I was just—

63
00:06:55,240 --> 00:06:56,004
It’s alright.

64
00:06:56,386 --> 00:06:57,503
You can keep looking.

65
00:06:58,454 --> 00:07:02,170
There are still so many things
I want you to know, Praew.

66
00:07:04,740 --> 00:07:06,499
Now that you know the whole truth,

67
00:07:07,444 --> 00:07:12,100
how do you think
all this crap should end, Praew?

68
00:07:26,568 --> 00:07:27,801
Okay.

69
00:07:32,150 --> 00:07:33,259
We’ve checked, sir.

70
00:07:33,300 --> 00:07:35,090
The car is a rental.

71
00:07:35,420 --> 00:07:38,404
Contact all checkpoints and tell them
to inspect every suspicious car.

72
00:07:38,560 --> 00:07:39,500
Yes, sir.

73
00:07:43,448 --> 00:07:44,496
What do we have?

74
00:07:45,450 --> 00:07:47,410
I don’t give a damn about some papers!

75
00:07:47,830 --> 00:07:51,600
Look through the playback footage
and look for the car I sent you.

76
00:07:51,800 --> 00:07:53,840
Send me the footage immediately.

77
00:07:54,343 --> 00:07:55,804
I’ll take responsibility for that.

78
00:07:57,040 --> 00:07:58,297
Check every intersection,

79
00:07:58,862 --> 00:08:01,202
and every street that crosses this area.

80
00:08:01,620 --> 00:08:02,800
(Yes, sir.)

81
00:08:03,364 --> 00:08:06,102
(I’m sending you the link
to the real-time footage right now.)

82
00:08:14,757 --> 00:08:17,800
(The suspected car
is heading out of the city, sir.)

83
00:08:42,961 --> 00:08:43,702
What?

84
00:08:54,222 --> 00:08:54,897
Praew?

85
00:08:56,540 --> 00:08:57,800
Why are you doing this?

86
00:08:59,580 --> 00:09:03,002
You should know better than anyone
why I’m doing this.

87
00:09:03,890 --> 00:09:06,001
That journalist is manipulating you.

88
00:09:07,190 --> 00:09:09,146
You’re misunderstanding me, Praew.

89
00:09:09,570 --> 00:09:10,499
No, she isn’t.

90
00:09:22,551 --> 00:09:25,100
The only reason you’re still breathing

91
00:09:25,863 --> 00:09:27,890
is all thanks to your niece.

92
00:09:28,400 --> 00:09:31,699
She asked me to spare you until now
so you can tell her the truth.

93
00:09:39,760 --> 00:09:44,271
Now I’ll let you talk and convince Praew,
however you can,

94
00:09:45,244 --> 00:09:48,102
that you’re really sorry about
all the crap that happened.

95
00:09:49,360 --> 00:09:50,597
And don’t lie.

96
00:09:52,650 --> 00:09:54,100
Because if you do,

97
00:09:55,306 --> 00:09:57,094
there won’t be a second chance.

98
00:10:06,730 --> 00:10:07,466
Praew.

99
00:10:08,214 --> 00:10:09,397
Listen to me.

100
00:10:10,002 --> 00:10:12,970
The truth isn’t what he’s trying
to make you think.

101
00:10:46,870 --> 00:10:49,060
Everything I did was to protect you.

102
00:10:50,327 --> 00:10:54,202
But it wasn’t without a condition.

103
00:10:55,023 --> 00:10:56,530
You need to let this case close.

104
00:10:56,600 --> 00:10:59,040
Forget it. Let it end.
20 YEARS AGO

105
00:10:59,080 --> 00:11:01,001
Don’t dig up anything again.

106
00:11:03,000 --> 00:11:04,496
I’m doing the right thing.

107
00:11:05,306 --> 00:11:07,450
It’s you
who need to stay out of this case.

108
00:11:08,872 --> 00:11:10,240
I won’t bow down to anyone.

109
00:11:10,671 --> 00:11:12,200
I don’t care what big shots they are.

110
00:11:13,146 --> 00:11:14,900
I know them better than you.

111
00:11:15,350 --> 00:11:17,998
If it was just your life on the line,
I wouldn’t get involved.

112
00:11:18,740 --> 00:11:21,100
But they will kill everyone you love
if you don’t stop.

113
00:11:26,500 --> 00:11:28,497
Between your family
and doing what is right,

114
00:11:29,410 --> 00:11:31,001
what is more important to you?

115
00:11:32,038 --> 00:11:33,250
Don’t say I didn’t warn you.

116
00:11:35,450 --> 00:11:36,601
But if I give up now,

117
00:11:37,962 --> 00:11:40,254
what will become of
the hundreds of families out there?

118
00:11:41,574 --> 00:11:44,602
How will you face them
even if you’re alive?

119
00:11:48,210 --> 00:11:49,743
(It’s a shock for the police department)

120
00:11:49,779 --> 00:11:52,750
(when Commissioner Praphaphat Traikanawut
and his wife)

121
00:11:52,790 --> 00:11:55,050
(were killed in a car accident.)

122
00:11:55,090 --> 00:11:57,111
He left behind a scandal
when it’s been revealed that

123
00:11:57,150 --> 00:12:01,580
an important evidence for the infamous
fraud case of Thai Investment Bank

124
00:12:01,623 --> 00:12:03,402
has mysteriously disappeared.

125
00:12:03,441 --> 00:12:06,339
It’s been suspected by the public
that it was Commissioner Praphaphat

126
00:12:06,380 --> 00:12:08,450
who had accepted a bribe
to get rid of the evidence

127
00:12:08,690 --> 00:12:10,897
(which allowed the executives
to walk free.)

128
00:12:12,360 --> 00:12:13,580
(The latest footage we have)

129
00:12:13,622 --> 00:12:16,608
(is of the car taking an exit
out of the main road.)

130
00:12:16,651 --> 00:12:18,299
(There are no traffic cameras
on the side road, sir.)

131
00:12:18,357 --> 00:12:19,960
Send me the latest coordinate.

132
00:12:36,131 --> 00:12:37,050
The truth.

133
00:12:37,637 --> 00:12:39,002
I only want the truth.

134
00:12:41,106 --> 00:12:42,300
Not excuses.

135
00:12:48,939 --> 00:12:51,202
I had to let your father die

136
00:12:52,152 --> 00:12:54,900
to save your and Phat’s lives.

137
00:12:57,230 --> 00:13:02,377
(They were powerful enough
to have your father killed and framed.)

138
00:13:05,349 --> 00:13:09,397
You stood by watching
our father die and take the blame

139
00:13:10,980 --> 00:13:13,195
while you lived on pretending
to be the good guy…

140
00:13:14,333 --> 00:13:15,600
How could you do that?

141
00:13:16,918 --> 00:13:20,398
Did Nop die for your secret, too?

142
00:13:22,056 --> 00:13:23,480
I had to let it happen.

143
00:13:27,770 --> 00:13:33,602
(If I didn’t, your father,
and every victim in that case,)

144
00:13:34,142 --> 00:13:35,530
(would have died for nothing.)

145
00:13:35,917 --> 00:13:40,001
(I had to do this
to make sure I had power.)

146
00:13:41,410 --> 00:13:43,800
(To have enough power to deal with them.)

147
00:13:44,389 --> 00:13:46,198
(Everything has a cost!)

148
00:14:07,788 --> 00:14:08,499
Hello.

149
00:14:08,720 --> 00:14:09,500
Kaye.

150
00:14:10,035 --> 00:14:12,002
Tell me where he is.

151
00:14:13,419 --> 00:14:14,702
(Kaye, please.)

152
00:14:15,440 --> 00:14:16,451
(Just tell me.)

153
00:14:16,940 --> 00:14:18,801
If you don’t stop them right now,

154
00:14:19,462 --> 00:14:21,770
Praew will become a murderer
just like Kim did.

155
00:14:23,379 --> 00:14:25,078
(Kaye, you’re the only one)

156
00:14:25,120 --> 00:14:26,798
who can stop this ending from happening.

157
00:14:27,210 --> 00:14:28,201
Tell me.

158
00:14:31,602 --> 00:14:35,496
And it’s almost time for them
to pay for what they did.

159
00:14:36,205 --> 00:14:37,402
Trust me, Praew.

160
00:14:49,560 --> 00:14:50,302
Praew.

161
00:15:02,728 --> 00:15:03,500
Praew.

162
00:15:07,954 --> 00:15:10,200
I’ve been hunting them all this time.

163
00:15:11,990 --> 00:15:13,352
But in the end, I learned that

164
00:15:13,390 --> 00:15:16,250
the worst of them
aren't those vile criminals,

165
00:15:16,770 --> 00:15:20,002
but the people who pride themselves
as protectors of laws

166
00:15:20,235 --> 00:15:22,200
who choose to stand with the devil.

167
00:15:22,780 --> 00:15:26,560
No wonder people like us
feel hopeless about justice.

168
00:15:27,087 --> 00:15:27,900
Good.

169
00:15:28,470 --> 00:15:29,899
Today, we will see

170
00:15:30,310 --> 00:15:33,503
what a true monster actually looks like.

171
00:15:38,696 --> 00:15:40,700
Praew, listen to me.

172
00:15:41,420 --> 00:15:45,490
You don’t have to feel guilty
about killing the likes of him.

173
00:15:46,430 --> 00:15:48,400
Just don’t think of them as human beings.

174
00:15:49,620 --> 00:15:51,204
Because what they did

175
00:15:53,303 --> 00:15:55,217
makes them lower than animals.

176
00:15:58,380 --> 00:16:02,300
The guests are going to be here soon,
but it seems we’re not ready.

177
00:16:03,026 --> 00:16:04,998
It’s time to drag him to his end.

178
00:16:12,653 --> 00:16:16,697
Praew, I’ll accept your decision.

179
00:16:19,016 --> 00:16:19,797
If…

180
00:16:23,438 --> 00:16:24,798
If you want me dead,

181
00:16:28,388 --> 00:16:29,697
I won’t refuse.

182
00:17:02,397 --> 00:17:04,410
Why did he want Praew
to send us the video?

183
00:17:04,842 --> 00:17:06,500
It’s a final invitation.

184
00:17:06,797 --> 00:17:10,474
An invitation to the execution
where you and I are the witnesses.

185
00:17:16,520 --> 00:17:17,248
Praew.

186
00:17:17,294 --> 00:17:20,699
Death would be too nice for you.

187
00:17:21,074 --> 00:17:22,810
You have to take responsibility
for what you did.

188
00:17:23,100 --> 00:17:25,650
You have to be branded
a dirty cop like Dad was.

189
00:17:25,995 --> 00:17:27,601
You will die in prison.

190
00:17:55,560 --> 00:17:56,862
You… jerk.

191
00:18:54,460 --> 00:18:56,010
You go this way. I’ll go that way.

192
00:18:56,536 --> 00:18:58,102
Okay. Be careful.

193
00:19:26,890 --> 00:19:27,902
Praew, Praew.

194
00:19:28,900 --> 00:19:29,734
Praew. Praew.
Praew.

195
00:19:32,500 --> 00:19:33,205
Praew.

196
00:19:37,522 --> 00:19:38,401
Kaye.

197
00:19:44,773 --> 00:19:46,902
Thun… Thun took my uncle.

198
00:19:49,565 --> 00:19:50,404
I got it.

199
00:19:53,450 --> 00:19:54,442
I’m coming with you.

200
00:19:57,320 --> 00:19:58,297
Listen to me, Praew.

201
00:19:59,020 --> 00:19:59,997
Stay here.

202
00:20:00,300 --> 00:20:01,303
Don’t go anywhere.

203
00:20:02,005 --> 00:20:03,097
It’s dangerous.

204
00:20:04,955 --> 00:20:05,903
I’ll handle this.

205
00:20:45,810 --> 00:20:47,102
Took you long enough.

206
00:20:51,669 --> 00:20:53,410
I believed in Praew.

207
00:20:54,330 --> 00:20:56,097
But it’s all ruined now.

208
00:20:57,860 --> 00:20:59,480
But what can we do, huh?

209
00:20:59,515 --> 00:21:00,760
The show must go on.

210
00:21:01,509 --> 00:21:02,398
Am I right?

211
00:21:04,835 --> 00:21:05,702
Enough now.

212
00:21:06,832 --> 00:21:08,177
It’s over now.

213
00:21:08,751 --> 00:21:12,290
And I believe Phat will make things right.

214
00:21:14,112 --> 00:21:15,200
Dai-sensei,

215
00:21:16,010 --> 00:21:18,496
I am the product from the tip of your pen.

216
00:21:19,568 --> 00:21:21,502
You wrote Nekros

217
00:21:22,825 --> 00:21:26,900
because you weren’t brave enough
to make it happen.

218
00:21:28,349 --> 00:21:32,300
I’m just turning your ink… into blood.

219
00:21:34,404 --> 00:21:35,299
Well?

220
00:21:35,948 --> 00:21:38,143
Is the ending you can see
with your own eyes

221
00:21:38,989 --> 00:21:40,880
even more beautiful than
what is on the page?

222
00:21:58,710 --> 00:21:59,697
Get up!

223
00:22:05,442 --> 00:22:06,198
Look.

224
00:22:06,920 --> 00:22:08,202
Look at this geezer!

225
00:22:09,398 --> 00:22:11,604
He’s lived a happy life for 20 years

226
00:22:12,170 --> 00:22:14,103
on the corpses of my parents,

227
00:22:14,770 --> 00:22:15,850
your parents,

228
00:22:16,711 --> 00:22:19,700
and thousands of victims of
the Thai Investment Bank case.

229
00:22:21,430 --> 00:22:23,042
People respect him.

230
00:22:23,682 --> 00:22:25,502
Laws protect him.

231
00:22:26,850 --> 00:22:28,801
Meanwhile, your father was a vegetable

232
00:22:29,509 --> 00:22:31,700
and mine hanged themselves.

233
00:22:32,813 --> 00:22:34,376
Where is justice?

234
00:22:34,610 --> 00:22:35,398
Where is it?

235
00:22:36,010 --> 00:22:36,798
Huh?

236
00:22:37,090 --> 00:22:37,900
Phat.

237
00:22:38,480 --> 00:22:39,697
Just shoot him!

238
00:22:41,730 --> 00:22:46,299
But killing him won’t bring
any of our parents back.

239
00:22:48,474 --> 00:22:51,370
It’s just going to turn us
into monsters like him.

240
00:22:52,565 --> 00:22:54,402
I am no monster, dai-sensei.

241
00:22:55,340 --> 00:22:57,000
I only stain my hands with blood

242
00:22:57,750 --> 00:22:59,856
in order to spread the truth,

243
00:23:00,220 --> 00:23:02,099
the very thing you didn’t
have the guts to do.

244
00:23:02,576 --> 00:23:05,496
And today, the end has come.

245
00:23:06,383 --> 00:23:08,900
What a fun freaking ending it is!

246
00:23:09,560 --> 00:23:13,345
I gotta say this story really
is diverting until the very last act.

247
00:23:17,983 --> 00:23:20,001
Hey, stay still.

248
00:23:21,905 --> 00:23:22,900
Now choose.

249
00:23:24,438 --> 00:23:26,400
In my hand is justice.

250
00:23:27,385 --> 00:23:29,402
In our Inspector’s hand are the laws.

251
00:23:30,487 --> 00:23:35,002
If I throw this lighter,
this scumbag dies.

252
00:23:35,585 --> 00:23:36,940
The world will be lighter.

253
00:23:37,905 --> 00:23:40,860
But if you shoot me, Inspector,
and save him,

254
00:23:41,451 --> 00:23:43,640
all the evidence will be gone by tomorrow.

255
00:23:44,509 --> 00:23:45,699
Choti is dead.

256
00:23:46,217 --> 00:23:47,601
Kitti is also dead.

257
00:23:49,377 --> 00:23:50,585
This jerk will walk free.

258
00:23:51,207 --> 00:23:53,699
And as a wronged hero, at that.

259
00:23:55,185 --> 00:23:56,899
Now why don’t you try and
tell me, Inspector,

260
00:23:57,194 --> 00:24:00,382
that what I just said isn’t true?

261
00:24:29,137 --> 00:24:32,000
What do you think
makes the world go round?

262
00:24:32,302 --> 00:24:33,099
Huh?

263
00:24:34,037 --> 00:24:37,496
You think it’s your stupid justice
that runs this world?

264
00:24:39,070 --> 00:24:39,897
Wrong!

265
00:24:41,438 --> 00:24:42,995
It runs on power!

266
00:24:43,202 --> 00:24:46,800
And I will have that power
beneath my goddamn feet!

267
00:24:50,431 --> 00:24:52,000
But I won’t let you die right now.

268
00:24:52,850 --> 00:24:55,574
I’ll keep you alive as a stepping stone
to a big promotion.

269
00:24:55,814 --> 00:24:56,798
Got it?

270
00:24:57,100 --> 00:24:57,900
Jerk!

271
00:25:15,939 --> 00:25:16,802
Look.

272
00:25:19,720 --> 00:25:22,602
Look what ending waits for someone
who thinks he can beat the system.

273
00:25:24,560 --> 00:25:26,099
Your father was just as stupid.

274
00:25:26,320 --> 00:25:27,502
That’s why he had to die.

275
00:25:33,780 --> 00:25:34,970
As for your family,

276
00:25:36,684 --> 00:25:39,995
and all the scums who died
because of the Thai Investment Bank…

277
00:25:40,619 --> 00:25:42,400
You think that was injustice?

278
00:25:42,539 --> 00:25:43,300
Huh!

279
00:25:43,623 --> 00:25:44,397
No!

280
00:25:45,029 --> 00:25:47,002
It was just the price you had to pay.

281
00:25:48,000 --> 00:25:51,272
You think the world is
beautiful and orderly

282
00:25:52,062 --> 00:25:53,702
because of clean hands?

283
00:25:55,510 --> 00:25:58,001
I sacrificed myself to carry that sin,

284
00:25:58,469 --> 00:25:59,703
stained my hands bloodied,

285
00:26:00,880 --> 00:26:02,601
to build this perfect system,

286
00:26:03,656 --> 00:26:05,770
to build a beautiful world
for you to live in.

287
00:26:06,755 --> 00:26:07,602
You…

288
00:26:09,380 --> 00:26:10,697
My beloved nephew Phat.

289
00:26:13,201 --> 00:26:15,002
If I couldn’t teach you,

290
00:26:18,342 --> 00:26:20,920
I’d rather send you to your father.

291
00:26:38,460 --> 00:26:39,703
K–Kaye…

292
00:26:46,918 --> 00:26:47,702
Kaye

293
00:26:52,349 --> 00:26:53,102
Kaye!

294
00:26:58,970 --> 00:26:59,804
Well?

295
00:27:02,682 --> 00:27:04,650
You gonna let us try and kill each other?

296
00:27:05,470 --> 00:27:06,299
Huh?

297
00:27:09,400 --> 00:27:12,201
Or are we gonna talk nicely
as uncle and nephew again?

298
00:27:14,645 --> 00:27:15,499
No.

299
00:27:17,776 --> 00:27:19,497
I can make this work for us.

300
00:27:20,669 --> 00:27:22,900
We can walk out of here
as heroes together.

301
00:27:24,900 --> 00:27:26,102
We can start over.

302
00:28:37,054 --> 00:28:38,302
It’s beautiful…

303
00:28:39,472 --> 00:28:40,602
Dai-sensei.

304
00:28:45,870 --> 00:28:46,699
Kaye.

305
00:28:52,256 --> 00:28:54,699
I wouldn’t let a good guy
like you lose, Phat.

306
00:28:55,670 --> 00:28:56,502
Kaye!

307
00:28:58,020 --> 00:29:00,908
Thank you for everything
you’ve done for me.

308
00:29:07,320 --> 00:29:08,930
Let me be the monster instead.

309
00:29:09,402 --> 00:29:10,198
Kaye!

310
00:29:12,346 --> 00:29:13,099
Kaye!

311
00:29:15,234 --> 00:29:16,062
Kaye!

312
00:29:25,560 --> 00:29:28,580
There is nothing more shocking
for the nation right now

313
00:29:28,620 --> 00:29:31,502
than the conclusion
to the Nekros serial murder case,

314
00:29:31,647 --> 00:29:33,930
which ended with a tragedy in the fire.

315
00:29:35,072 --> 00:29:36,226
There’s a fire.

316
00:29:36,260 --> 00:29:37,114
Look at the smoke.
Please do not enter.

317
00:29:39,680 --> 00:29:41,010
Oh look. Someone’s injured.

318
00:29:41,472 --> 00:29:42,702
They’re carrying someone out.

319
00:29:43,331 --> 00:29:48,130
(Commissioner Chaiwat, the killer’s
last victim, made it out alive,)

320
00:29:48,527 --> 00:29:50,601
(although with partial burns.)

321
00:29:50,920 --> 00:29:54,002
(But the earth-shattering truth
lies with the revelation that)

322
00:29:54,211 --> 00:29:58,099
(Thun, the sensational journalist,
was the Nekros serial killer,)

323
00:29:58,322 --> 00:30:01,680
(who has been confirmed
to die in the fire.)

324
00:30:08,750 --> 00:30:10,703
(The end has come after 20 years.)

325
00:30:10,880 --> 00:30:14,770
Commissioner Chaiwat Traikanawut
has been arrested

326
00:30:15,001 --> 00:30:19,600
(after a video from Thunwikorn
was revealed.)

327
00:30:20,650 --> 00:30:22,662
(The evidence uncovers that
the Commissioner was responsible)

328
00:30:22,697 --> 00:30:25,650
(for silencing witnesses
and tampering evidence)

329
00:30:25,690 --> 00:30:27,097
(in the Thai Investment case)

330
00:30:27,373 --> 00:30:31,097
(as well as abusing his power
for more than two decades.)

331
00:30:31,499 --> 00:30:33,660
The situation has sent a big ripple
through the public,

332
00:30:33,700 --> 00:30:36,828
making people question the justice system,

333
00:30:36,874 --> 00:30:40,730
and leading to a reform regarding
corruption in the police department.

334
00:31:09,462 --> 00:31:11,400
Alright. You can move the stuff in.

335
00:31:11,497 --> 00:31:12,570
Just place them there.

336
00:31:15,010 --> 00:31:16,170
Uh, excuse me.

337
00:31:16,208 --> 00:31:17,720
Are you here to see someone?

338
00:31:18,520 --> 00:31:19,398
Oh…

339
00:31:19,628 --> 00:31:22,197
Did the previous tenant
take all his stuff?

340
00:31:22,377 --> 00:31:25,440
Actually, the landlord just
had to throw everything out.

341
00:31:25,598 --> 00:31:27,370
I just got a chance to come in
and clean the place up myself.

342
00:31:28,900 --> 00:31:29,700
Right.

343
00:31:31,010 --> 00:31:33,500
Guys, come on.
There are still boxes to unload.

344
00:31:45,537 --> 00:31:47,000
Why not just adopt them?

345
00:31:47,340 --> 00:31:48,598
It’s better this way.

346
00:31:49,677 --> 00:31:51,202
If one day I’m gone,

347
00:31:52,260 --> 00:31:53,801
someone will take care of them.

348
00:32:42,520 --> 00:32:47,602
(This is the last video taken
before his death.)

349
00:32:47,902 --> 00:32:49,602
Hey, you mind turning up the volume?

350
00:32:53,208 --> 00:32:55,400
(The world always asks:)

351
00:32:56,272 --> 00:32:58,063
(How makes a monster?)

352
00:32:59,080 --> 00:32:59,691
LAST CONFESSION FROM THUNWIKORN PUTTHANA

353
00:32:59,691 --> 00:33:04,057
(Is it genetics or a personal decay?)
LAST CONFESSION FROM THUNWIKORN PUTTHANA

354
00:33:04,057 --> 00:33:04,690
LAST CONFESSION FROM THUNWIKORN PUTTHANA

355
00:33:07,550 --> 00:33:08,401
(But no.)

356
00:33:09,280 --> 00:33:11,004
(A monster is not born on its own.)

357
00:33:12,200 --> 00:33:15,604
(It is born of your ignorance.)

358
00:33:16,460 --> 00:33:20,097
(20 years ago, the national fraud case
led by the Thai Investment Bank)

359
00:33:21,114 --> 00:33:23,499
(robbed my family of everything we had.)

360
00:33:24,911 --> 00:33:27,000
(The people in power leeched off of us)

361
00:33:27,477 --> 00:33:29,530
(and walked away
with spring in their steps.)

362
00:33:30,060 --> 00:33:32,065
(Meanwhile, victims like my parents…)

363
00:33:32,899 --> 00:33:35,002
were cornered by the laws

364
00:33:36,075 --> 00:33:38,500
until their backs were against the wall.

365
00:33:39,880 --> 00:33:42,053
That day, I screamed
at the top of my lungs,

366
00:33:42,560 --> 00:33:43,997
but no one heard me.

367
00:33:44,832 --> 00:33:48,060
Not a single good Samaritan
reached out their hand.

368
00:33:49,293 --> 00:33:53,703
Because they all kept one eye closed
and chose to believe the lie

369
00:33:54,576 --> 00:33:56,610
that the laws could take care of it.

370
00:33:59,637 --> 00:34:01,302
“Let the laws take care of it”?

371
00:34:03,011 --> 00:34:04,401
That day never came.

372
00:34:05,940 --> 00:34:07,598
Then I came across Nekros.

373
00:34:09,091 --> 00:34:10,903
It was a wake-up call for me.

374
00:34:11,831 --> 00:34:16,057
In the end, lies become truths

375
00:34:16,814 --> 00:34:20,850
if the people who know the truth
like you choose to stay silent.

376
00:34:20,880 --> 00:34:22,210
LOAN SHARKS MIX-UP: HOMEOWNER FIGHTS BACK

377
00:34:22,230 --> 00:34:23,053
MAN SHOT AFTER SAVING FRIEND
FROM LOAN SHARKS

378
00:34:23,053 --> 00:34:27,602
(Nekros is simply the scream
you pretend not to hear.)

379
00:34:29,749 --> 00:34:31,502
(My death isn’t the end.)

380
00:34:32,494 --> 00:34:36,798
It’s a question that is forever
ingrained in your brain:

381
00:34:39,122 --> 00:34:42,102
Between a killer who calls for justice

382
00:34:43,032 --> 00:34:46,063
and the unjust system
that kills its victim slowly,

383
00:34:48,150 --> 00:34:52,062
which of these is the actual monster?

384
00:35:17,920 --> 00:35:20,690
PRAPAPHAT TRAIKANAWUT / MEVIKA TRAIKANAWUT

385
00:36:44,130 --> 00:36:44,983
Prim?

386
00:36:45,240 --> 00:36:46,097
Prim.

387
00:36:56,400 --> 00:36:59,290
ONE YEAR LATER

388
00:37:07,940 --> 00:37:08,896
Oh, hey.

389
00:37:09,103 --> 00:37:10,650
Prim is waiting for me. I’m off.

390
00:37:11,257 --> 00:37:12,408
I might be home late tonight.

391
00:37:12,450 --> 00:37:13,801
We’ve got so much work to do.

392
00:37:14,040 --> 00:37:14,802
Umm.

393
00:37:16,762 --> 00:37:21,001
Oh, your favorite manga was just updated.

394
00:37:24,550 --> 00:37:25,902
Bye. See you.

395
00:39:01,739 --> 00:39:04,899
(All this time we ask who the monster is,)

396
00:39:06,090 --> 00:39:09,900
(we forget to ask how to stop
creating another monster.)

397
00:39:14,430 --> 00:39:16,995
(Monsters don’t just hide in the shadows.)

398
00:39:17,672 --> 00:39:21,401
(They also feed on every time
injustice goes unchecked,)

399
00:39:22,005 --> 00:39:24,450
(as we tell ourselves
it’s none of our business.)

400
00:39:25,560 --> 00:39:28,400
(Don’t let anyone fight alone.)

401
00:39:29,074 --> 00:39:32,197
(Because the day people
stop cowering in fears,)

402
00:39:32,620 --> 00:39:35,197
(that is the day change can happen)

403
00:39:35,680 --> 00:39:37,896
(and truth never dies)

404
00:39:38,231 --> 00:39:39,973
(as well as trust,)

405
00:39:40,041 --> 00:39:45,097
(which will find a way to rise again
even as the world burns.)

406
00:40:01,813 --> 00:40:02,598
Kaye?

407
00:40:07,440 --> 00:40:08,604
Is something the matter?

408
00:40:09,038 --> 00:40:10,600
I’m sorry.

409
00:40:11,411 --> 00:40:12,690
I thought you were someone I know.

410
00:40:13,420 --> 00:40:14,297
No problem.

411
00:41:04,509 --> 00:41:05,801
Nekros ended.

412
00:41:07,813 --> 00:41:09,201
What are you going to write now,

413
00:41:09,764 --> 00:41:10,697
Mr. Mangaka?

414
00:41:13,090 --> 00:41:15,097
I don’t know yet.

415
00:41:16,765 --> 00:41:20,850
I don’t even know
if people would read what I write.

416
00:41:21,500 --> 00:41:22,496
Of course they would.

417
00:41:23,060 --> 00:41:24,001
At least I will.

418
00:41:25,200 --> 00:41:27,066
But I’m asking this as a fan,

419
00:41:28,505 --> 00:41:31,100
can’t the next one be something
with a happy ending?

420
00:41:39,131 --> 00:41:40,069
Well then,

421
00:41:41,120 --> 00:41:44,800
I guess you’ll have to
help me write it, Inspector.

422
00:41:46,990 --> 00:41:47,871
Of course.

423
00:41:59,364 --> 00:42:01,804
I’m happy to see you again.

424
00:42:06,217 --> 00:42:07,100
So am I.

425
00:43:11,840 --> 00:43:15,810
THERE IS A POST-CREDIT SCENE.

426
00:44:26,070 --> 00:44:27,097
You have a lighter?
